WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.074
The children sat huddled under a tree.

2
00:00:04.075 --> 00:00:08.330
They were cold and hungry and had no place to go.

3
00:00:08.331 --> 00:00:12.068
"I want to go home." Jane shivered.

4
00:00:12.069 --> 00:00:17.001
"It's no fun being pretty if no one knows who you are."

5
00:00:17.002 --> 00:00:21.820
"It's getting dark," Bobby said, pointing to the sky.

6
00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.427
"What are we going to do?"

7
00:00:24.428 --> 00:00:29.472
The children watched miserably as the sun began to go down.

8
00:00:29.473 --> 00:00:32.794
"Wait a minute," Cy blurted.

9
00:00:32.795 --> 00:00:34.981
"Do you feel that?"

10
00:00:34.982 --> 00:00:42.033
They all felt a light mist on their faces, just as they had felt when they were with Huey that morning.

11
00:00:42.034 --> 00:00:45.619
They looked at each other cautiously.

12
00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.749
"Panther! It's you!" Cy shouted joyfully.

13
00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:56.115
Exactly as Huey had said, the wish had ended as soon as the sun was set.

14
00:00:56.116 --> 00:01:01.194
"Oh, I'm so happy to be me again!" Panther cried.

15
00:01:01.195 --> 00:01:03.565
Bobby added, "Me too.

16
00:01:03.566 --> 00:01:07.691
Now let's go home and get something to eat!"

17
00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:12.223
Aunt Martha was waiting by the door when the children got home.

18
00:01:12.224 --> 00:01:19.866
"Am I ever glad to see you," she said, giving them each a big hug and kiss.

19
00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:24.384
She told them about the strange kids who had broken into the house.

20
00:01:24.385 --> 00:01:28.490
"I nearly had a heart attack," she exclaimed.

21
00:01:28.491 --> 00:01:32.245
"How they knew my name, I'll never know."

22
00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:35.674
Dinner that evening was unusually quiet.

23
00:01:35.675 --> 00:01:40.921
The children were careful not to say anything about Huey or their wish.

24
00:01:40.922 --> 00:01:44.718
But once they were alone, they all spoke at once.

25
00:01:44.719 --> 00:01:46.926
Cy held up his hand.

26
00:01:46.927 --> 00:01:52.323
"Wait, wait," he said. "Panther, you go first."

27
00:01:52.324 --> 00:01:58.011
"I want to say that I'm sorry about today," she said quietly.

28
00:01:58.012 --> 00:02:01.610
"And I don't think we should go see Huey anymore."

29
00:02:01.611 --> 00:02:03.573
The others disagreed.

30
00:02:03.574 --> 00:02:06.923
"That's not fair," complained Bobby.

31
00:02:06.924 --> 00:02:09.962
"I haven't had my wish yet."

32
00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:13.971
"Yeah, I want a wish, too," whined Jane.

33
00:02:13.972 --> 00:02:19.596
"I think it's only fair for each of us to have at least one wish," Cy agreed.

34
00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:22.459
"So tomorrow, I'll go first─ "

35
00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:27.379
"Hey, why do you get to go first?" interrupted Bobby.

36
00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.399
"Because I'm the oldest," said Cy.

37
00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.050
"Next will be Bobby, and then Jane, okay?"

38
00:02:34.051 --> 00:02:36.714
The others nodded their heads.

39
00:02:36.715 --> 00:02:42.074
Bright and early the next morning, the children set off to see Huey.

40
00:02:42.075 --> 00:02:45.237
"Well, well." Huey grinned.

41
00:02:45.238 --> 00:02:49.153
"How did it feel to be handsome and beautiful?"

42
00:02:49.154 --> 00:02:53.618
"Fine, thank you," Panther answered quickly and untruthfully.

43
00:02:53.619 --> 00:02:56.908
"So what will you wish for today?"

44
00:02:56.909 --> 00:03:01.916
he said, shaking out his fins and swiveling his head.

45
00:03:01.917 --> 00:03:07.485
"I wish," Cy said excitedly, "we were rich."

46
00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:10.427
"How rich?" Huey asked.

47
00:03:10.428 --> 00:03:15.964
Cy scratched his head. "Uh, well . . ."

48
00:03:15.965 --> 00:03:18.335
Huey pointed to the bucket.

49
00:03:18.336 --> 00:03:21.978
"Enough money to fill this?" he asked.

50
00:03:21.979 --> 00:03:27.749
Cy rubbed his hands and said, "Twenty of those buckets, please."

51
00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:32.092
"And would you like gold? Silver?" asked Huey.

52
00:03:32.093 --> 00:03:35.017
Cy scratched his head again.

53
00:03:35.018 --> 00:03:37.313
"Gold," he answered.

54
00:03:37.314 --> 00:03:42.832
Huey spread his fins and they turned bright gold.

55
00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:47.940
"Wow," Bobby whispered under his breath.

56
00:03:47.941 --> 00:03:55.108
Like magic, twenty buckets appeared, and then gold coins showered down from the sky.

57
00:03:55.109 --> 00:03:59.399
"It's raining gold!" squealed Jane.

58
00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:01.808
"How are we going to carry all this?"

59
00:04:01.809 --> 00:04:07.498
Cy asked, pointing to the buckets now filled with shining coins.

60
00:04:07.499 --> 00:04:12.672
Closing his fins, Huey said, "That's your problem."

61
00:04:12.673 --> 00:04:15.575
He ducked back into his shell.

62
00:04:15.576 --> 00:04:21.517
"Don't forget—it'll all be gone by sunset," he added.

63
00:04:21.518 --> 00:04:28.268
Cy lowered Huey down the well, and the children started to fill their pockets with the gold.

64
00:04:28.269 --> 00:04:31.421
"Take as much as you can," Cy urged.

65
00:04:31.422 --> 00:04:35.210
"The more the better."

